        "title": "UNESCO HERITAGE PASHUPATHINATH TEMPLE",
        "text": "It is a famous, sacred Hindu temple dedicated to Pashupatinath and is located on the banks of the Bagmati River 5 kilometres north-east of Kathmandu Valley in the eastern city of KMT. \nThis temple complex is on UNESCO World Heritage Sites's list Since 1979.\nInnermost part of the temple is only reserved for true Hindus!\nAll the rituals are active and alive.\nCrowded always!\nA few remarkable scars of 2015 earthquake are evidently still there.\nOne interesting and love to observe is a lot of vendors along the entrance way to the temple.\nAll have their own peculiarities, colours, fragrances, movements, sounds, etc.",
