        "title": "Wonderful walking tour in a fascinating place",
        "text": "My visit to Pashupatinath was made all the more worthwhile by experiencing it with a guide - Sumit Kharel, who I met at the entrance of the temple complex. Sumit was very knowledgeable, friendly, good-humoured and spoke impressive English, and I learned a lot more than I would have if I had explored the site alone. The Pashupatinath temple complex is a fascinating and extensive place, and it was enlightening to have a local explain the various Hindu customs and rituals of life and death unfolding before our eyes in an engaging way. Sumit was also kind enough to show me around the equally impressive Boudhanath stupa, a towering Buddhist monument.\nIf you want to gain valuable insights into this wonderful spiritual place, its history and its culture, I highly recommend hiring Sumit as your guide.",
