        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r407065901-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Get a guide...",
        "text": "The area looks very interesting, but without some background knowledge about the things going on there you only get like 10% of the experience. We highly recommend Sumit Kharel as a guide - you can ask for him at the entrance (or ask some of the elderly people around, he's good friends with all of them it seems), if he doesn't grab you right away as he did with us. He knows a lot, knows a little german, is learning chinese and answers pretty much any questions you may have regarding nepali culture and religion. He also shows you the best places to take pictures and gives you all the time you need. No hurry and a whole bunch of information at one of the most interesting places in Kathmandu. Worth every rupee.",
