        "title": "Don't know what to say",
        "text": "First of all the entrance fee for people from the western counties is 1000 rupees which is discriminating (for others is about 250 rupees) in my opinion. \nSecond, even one year after the earthquake they did absolutely nothing to rebuild the place. UNESCO should definitely do something about it.\nThird, is totally absurd they showing their funeral traditions to the tourist. On one side there are families which cry and on the other side there are tourists who take photos. Absolutely crazy.\nFourth, you can't even see the main Golden temple, it's only reserved for Hindu people (even though you paid 1000 rupees).\nFifth, be careful with people who represent as tourist guides, they would just start walking by you explaining the place (event though you didn't ask them anything) and in the end they want money from you. \nAnd the last, be aware and careful when taking pictures whit 'holy people' there - they what money after taking pictures (they wanted 1000 rupees from each of us).",
